From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 05:42:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 391/394] dt-bindings: soc: mediatek: add the MT6797 CONSYS
 owner

CONSYS owns what the MT6797 connectivity functions share: the
boot-allocated no-map firmware reservation, the CONN power domain, the
CONMCU reset, the BTIF transport that carries WMT, the connectivity
analog front-end and the AHB host interface of the WLAN function.

The binding describes the complete start chain as the device's normal
behaviour. The station series selected each stage with an experimental
one-shot-* or deferred-* property; those properties are gone, and the
resources the chain uses (all eleven register ranges, both clocks, the
interrupt, the Bluetooth 3.3 V supply and the coexistence antenna mode)
are required.

Part of the clean MT6797 Wi-Fi series (Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 1).
